    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 4.6,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.99,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.92–0.97 from 6 h onward. That flat line looks like reader saturation. Diluting the 18 h aliquot shows a much higher density. At 10-fold dilution the reads were 0.481 and 0.475, which corresponds to about 4.8 OD undiluted. At 20-fold dilution the read was 0.228, which corresponds to about 4.55 OD. The two dilutions agree reasonably well. The 20-fold value is probably the more reliable one, since the 10-fold read at about 0.48 may already be slightly compressed. The true 18 h OD is therefore about 4.5–4.8, roughly 5 times the undiluted reading of about 0.92. Growth most likely continued past 6 h while the undiluted reading stayed capped."
  },
